//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eratosthenes"},{"title":"Library of Alexandria","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Library_of_Alexandria"}]},{"text":"People used home-made balloons and submarines to escape across the inner German border between East and West Germany during the Cold War.","sources":[{"title":"Balloon","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Balloon"},{"title":"Submarine","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Submarine"},{"title":"Inner German border","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Inner_German_border"},{"title":"East Germany","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/East_Germany"},{"title":"West Germany","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/West_Germany"},{"title":"Cold War","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cold_War"}]}],"fake":0,"original":"The medieval Margraviate of Brandenburg was called \"the sandbox of the Holy Roman Empire\".","change":{"kind":"what","old":"the sandbox","new":"the breadbasket","start":52,"end":63},"difficulty":1.0,"nli":0.8725,"fact_ids":["2e10297bfd42","412ddf09c026","530452aabbf9","b0fe939b241a","29ec48d4cd31"]},{"facts":[{"text":"The Wachau in Austria inspired the name of the Wachovia area in North Carolina.","sources":[{"title":"Wachau","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wachau"},{"title":"Austria","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Austria"},{"title":"Wachovia Tract","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wachovia_Tract"},{"title":"North Carolina","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/North_Carolina"}]},{"text":"The French clothing brand Cacharel is named after a wild horse that inhabits the Camargue.","sources":[{"title":"France","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/France"},{"title":"Cacharel","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cacharel"},{"title":"Camargue","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Camargue"}]},{"text":"After the destructive Byzantine civil war of 1341–1347, the treasury of the Byzantine Empire contained \"nothing but the atoms of Epicurus\".","sources":[{"title":"Byzantine civil war of 1341–1347","url":"htt