dia.org/wiki/Stirlingshire"},{"title":"Hungary","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hungary"}]},{"text":"Jain figure Bahubali is said to have meditated motionless in a standing posture for a year, during which time climbing plants grew around his legs.","sources":[{"title":"Jainism","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jainism"},{"title":"Bahubali","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bahubali"}]},{"text":"Whipcracking, the art of using a whip to create a miniature sonic boom, is a competitive sport in Australia, where it was also elaborated into whipboxing.","sources":[{"title":"Whipcracking","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Whipcracking"},{"title":"Whip","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Whip"},{"title":"Sonic boom","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sonic_boom"},{"title":"Australia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Australia"},{"title":"Whip fighting","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Whip_fighting"}]},{"text":"The word \"agnosticism\" was coined by biologist Thomas Henry Huxley.","sources":[{"title":"Agnosticism","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Agnosticism"},{"title":"Thomas Henry Huxley","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thomas_Henry_Huxley"}]}],"fake":1,"original":"Tradition traces Clan Drummond, a Scottish clan from Stirlingshire, to Hungarian origins.","change":{"kind":"where","old":"Hungarian origins","new":"Norwegian origins","start":71,"end":88},"difficulty":1.0,"nli":0.9955,"fact_ids":["be044d2f4a9b","4fd7886f7b9f","0a8ae3b78359","be43509846a7","b0f9e17bc5ba"]}]}